# PART 17 — TESTING AND VALIDATION

Do not mark a feature complete because its interface exists.

Test actual functionality.

At minimum, verify these workflows:

### Workflow A — Character import

Import an HTML character, inspect its compatibility, add it to the viewport, manipulate it and save the project.

### Workflow B — Curved movement

Select a character, create a multi-point Bézier path, edit its handles, animate the character along the path and preview the result.

### Workflow C — Body-part animation

Select an individual arm, create rotation keyframes, animate the arm and verify the rest of the character is not unintentionally transformed.

### Workflow D — IK

Move a hand target and verify that the arm responds correctly where a compatible rig exists.

### Workflow E — Timeline

Create keyframes for position, rotation and facial expression. Move, duplicate, delete and edit them. Verify that playback reflects the changes.

### Workflow F — Graph editor

Change an animation curve and verify that the resulting movement changes accordingly.

### Workflow G — Multiple characters

Animate several characters simultaneously with independent paths, animation tracks and audio configurations.

### Workflow H — Dialogue

Assign different dialogue to two characters, preview the audio and verify synchronization.

### Workflow I — Production

Create multiple scenes, animate them, add camera movements and export a finished video.

### Workflow J — Persistence

Save, close and reopen a project. Verify that characters, animations, keyframes, paths, audio assignments and scenes remain intact.

Add unit tests, integration tests and browser-based interaction tests wherever practical.

Fix regressions before moving forward.

